ptions":["Variance and standard deviation","Mean and median","Mode and median only","Skewness and kurtosis only"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"f028e1e085dc919ffc7753c5","time_limit":20},{"id":"pt_batch10_summary_measures_of_a_distribution_008","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"application","question":"Which pair summarizes shape features of a loss distribution?","options":["Mean and median","Skewness and kurtosis","Variance and standard deviation","Minimum and maximum only"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"b3e997e38c5d7d54b389cd91","time_limit":20},{"id":"pt_batch10_summary_measures_of_a_distribution_009","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"application","question":"If two distributions have the same mean but one has much larger variance, which summary differs?","options":["Center only","Total probability","The event space only","Spread"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"e5835df2ff5c6ae675eb705b","time_limit":20},{"id":"pt_batch10_summary_measures_of_a_distribution_010","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"application","question":"If a distribution is strongly right-skewed, which kind of summary is being described?","options":["Location only","Sample size","Shape","Probability total"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"7723c14e214957b57823a480","time_limit":20},{"id":"pt_batch10_summary_measures_of_a_distribution_011","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"conceptual","question":"Why is no single summary measure enough to describe a distribution fully?","options":["All summaries are identical","Distributions have no features beyond the mean","Center, spread, and shape capture different features","Only probabilities of exact points matter"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"0228b959c0e82eae018fbe51","time_limit":30},{"id":"pt_batch10_summary_measures_of_a_distribution_012","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"conceptual","question":"How do summary measures condense a distribution?","options":["They 