85ce682bb","time_limit":30},{"id":"pt_batch10_summary_measures_of_a_distribution_017","difficulty":"challenge","question_type":"conceptual","question":"What misconception comes from comparing distributions only by their means?","options":["It uses too many summaries","It always reveals tail behavior","No misconception arises because the mean alone determines the whole distribution","It ignores spread and shape differences"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"7615b3fff07ea3dc36b466b7","time_limit":40},{"id":"pt_batch10_summary_measures_of_a_distribution_018","difficulty":"challenge","question_type":"conceptual","question":"Why are summary measures not a substitute for all distributional information?","options":["Different distributions can share the same summaries","Summaries always uniquely determine every distribution","Summaries contain every probability value","Summary measures cannot be numerical"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"731245a0090aed97771d23c4","time_limit":40},{"id":"pt_batch10_summary_measures_of_a_distribution_019","difficulty":"challenge","question_type":"application","question":"Two demand distributions have equal variance but one is strongly skewed. Which summary type distinguishes them?","options":["Shape measures","Spread measures only","Location measures only","Sample size measures"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"31abb2799945966683df10ec","time_limit":40},{"id":"pt_batch10_summary_measures_of_a_distribution_020","difficulty":"challenge","question_type":"application","question":"A report lists only standard deviation to describe delivery times. What important feature might still be missing?","options":["Total probability, which must exceed one","Center or shape information","The fact that standard deviation is numerical","The sample path of a process"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"aaf2f598de0da243ee874cdb","time_limit":40}]}}